Third-party exceptions

A subset of the entries in tags.csv and tags.dmap were derived from
third-party sources with their own licenses. These entries are identified
by their `sources` field and are NOT covered by the CC0 dedication — they
retain their original upstream terms:

  pydicom / GDCM-derived entries  (sources = ["pydicom"])
  -------------------------------------------------------
  Entries bearing sources=["pydicom"] were imported from pydicom's bundled
  private dictionary (pydicom/_private_dict.py). The module header states:
  "Data generated from GDCM project's private dictionary." A review of
  pydicom's git history confirms the vast majority of entries are GDCM-derived;
  a small number of corrections and additions were made directly by pydicom
  contributors (e.g. TOSHIBA_MEC_MR3^10, several MITRA family corrections in
  2021–2022). No per-entry provenance flag exists in pydicom's source — a
  finer-grained split between GDCM-origin and pydicom-origin is not possible
  from the published data alone.

  Note on the license type: MIT and BSD-3-Clause are software licenses, not
